    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.14,
      "end_seconds": 172.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.39,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. I swim twice a week. I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.18,
      "end_seconds": 184.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.01,
      "end_seconds": 197.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "Um I've had asthma yes. I've had anxiety yes. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.71,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.05,
      "end_seconds": 221.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.47,
      "end_seconds": 224.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.29,
      "end_seconds": 243.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.3,
      "end_seconds": 262.36,
      "duration_seconds": 13.06,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. So where does that leave us? It fits best with episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. It could also be atrial fibrillation, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.91,
      "end_seconds": 265.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.01,
      "end_seconds": 273.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like episodes of supraventricular tachycardia, but I'd like to confirm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 276.38,
      "end_seconds": 280.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I've already done an ECG, it's ready for you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.43,
      "end_seconds": 296.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.33,
      "text": "right, thank you try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.34,
      "end_seconds": 299.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "I understand"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.32,
      "end_seconds": 307.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.11,
      "end_seconds": 310.73,
